/*
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Per-task TMPDIR (included from nextflow.config when params.task_tmpdir is true)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Points each task's TMPDIR at a `tmp/` directory inside its own work dir.

    Nextflow forwards the host's TMPDIR into Apptainer/Singularity containers
    (APPTAINERENV_TMPDIR), but only mounts the task work dir (and runs with
    --no-home). A host TMPDIR outside those mounts - e.g. under $HOME - then
    doesn't exist inside the container, and any tool writing temporary files
    fails (seen with `samtools collate` in DEHOST: "Cannot open intermediate
    file"). The work dir is always mounted, on the same filesystem as the rest
    of the run's data, and cleaned up with it.

    The value is evaluated by the task's own shell, inside the container, so
    $PWD is the task work dir; the command substitution creates the directory.

    Short path when the work dir path is long: Unix socket paths are limited
    to ~107 characters, and Python's multiprocessing (e.g. CheckM2) creates
    its manager socket under $TMPDIR (TMPDIR/pymp-XXXXXXXX/listener-XXXXXXXX,
    ~32 more characters), failing with "OSError: AF_UNIX path too long" once
    <work dir>/tmp passes ~75 characters - typical on a cluster. So when it's
    longer than 70 characters, TMPDIR is a short symlink,
    /tmp/nxf-<task hash>, pointing at <work dir>/tmp: the socket path stays
    short, but files still land in the work dir. /tmp is writable on the host
    (conda/local), bound by default in Apptainer/Singularity, and the
    container's own in Docker. If the symlink can't be made, it falls back to
    the full path. The symlinks are left behind in /tmp (one tiny link per
    task with a long work dir; none under Docker).

    Disable with `task_tmpdir = false` (e.g. in a -params-file) to keep the
    host's TMPDIR instead.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*/

env {
    TMPDIR = '$(d="$PWD/tmp"; mkdir -p "$d"; s="/tmp/nxf-$(basename "$(dirname "$PWD")")$(basename "$PWD")"; if [ ${#d} -gt 70 ] && ln -sfn "$d" "$s" 2>/dev/null; then echo "$s"; else echo "$d"; fi)'
}
